f F,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F} = \\langle x, \\,0, \\, -y^2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand the closed surface $S$ that represents the boundary of the conical solid shown below. \n\n![](images/0b/0be83ceada68d0b56be4872f21652a7d18932ff059ea704576ca3cce892fa87b.png)\n\n \n\nLet's calculate the flux of $\\mathbf F$ through $S.$ \n\nFirst, since $S$ is a closed surface, we have that\n\n- the upper surface $S_1: z = g(x,y) = 2 - \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}$ is oriented *upward*, and\n\n- the lower surface $S_2: z = h(x,y) = 0$ is oriented *downward*.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- First, we consider the upper cone $S_1.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $\\mathbf{F}=\\langle P, \\, Q, \\, R \\rangle,$ then\n\n$$\nP = x, \\qquad\nQ = 0, \\qquad\nR = -y^2.\n$$\n\n \nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-x\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})-0\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})+(-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane.\n\n- Next, we consider the lower plane $S_2.$ \n\nSince the positive orientation is downward, the unit normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n} = \\langle 0,0,-1 \\rangle.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨x,0,-{y}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ across the entire surface is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199468 #edb/ref 1065 7651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199468 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "73467c61-810e-5e81-abcc-b5eb99d1e0ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199468 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278645 #edb/ref 1080 "-2{x}^{3}+4x{y}^{2}+4x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278645 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278645 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05c9ad26-77bc-5b7f-828d-2c0cdf073e56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278717 #edb/ref 1080 "-4{x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}+6x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278717 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278717 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d747dec-4db3-5966-9a2d-772570a4c2a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278753 #edb/ref 1080 "-2{x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}+10x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278753 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278753 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1152644c-483e-593c-b840-d414f08e1c17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278839 #edb/ref 1080 "2x-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278839 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278839 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1b0db8ab-29d7-5fe3-9f20-8a503e358b7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278851 #edb/ref 1080 "2{x}^{2}y+2{y}^{3}-6y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278851 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278851 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1c3047a2-d5df-5a0c-ab0c-a0f194bdad31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278971 #edb/ref 1080 "y-x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278971 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 1759218604541