5687db48171819e1efaa858701af881ebbee57ff835da569f30947.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=⟨{z}^{2},\\,0,\\,y⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that represents the boundary of the solid shown above. Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich expression belongs in the blank when the upper and lower surfaces are parametrized as graphs over $D$ and their outward flux integrands are added pointwise where defined, before integration?" #edb/ref 17592186045423] [17592186405083 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3eea45a-e598-5192-b757-2e1b9a1153d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405083 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So, \n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=0$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper hemisphere ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP={z}^{2}=4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,Q=0,\\,R=y.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-(4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}})-0\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}})+y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the lower plane ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nSince the positive orientation is downward, the unit normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,0,-1⟩.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨{z}^{2},0,y⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux of $F$ across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+y\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}-y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186405085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405084 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "55ff700f-c93e-5ab0-80b1-0ec031f0502f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405085 #edb/ref 1080 "x\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405085 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405085 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "263b1feb-971b-5d7f-8e46-5b3bc0e94dcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405086 #edb/ref 1080 "y\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405086 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405086 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb4e563f-2961-582e-92cd-4ac00f3541da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405087 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405087 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405087 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "94cdc7b9-f47b-525c-b5b6-ab08d22fded3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405088 #edb/ref 1080 "xy\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405088 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405088 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "34969a97-52a8-5790-8d57-5135e6098783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405089 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405089 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405089 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c701af60-222c-5761-9908-aa65b644b188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405090 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186405091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405090 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161903" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405090 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405090 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $F=⟨0,\\,-z,\\,2y⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that encloses the finite region between the cone $z=4-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and the plane $z=0.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich expression belongs in the blank when the upper and lower surfaces are parametrized as graphs over $D$ and their outward flux integrands are added pointwise where defined, before integration?" #edb/ref 17592186045423] [17592186405090 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c8fd3ad8-a86b-542f-ab4a-6226468a4f6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405090 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=4-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=0$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper cone ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=-z=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4,\\,R=2y.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(0)\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})-(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})+2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y-\\frac{4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3y-\\frac{4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider lower plane ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nSince the positive orientation is downward, the unit normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,0,-1⟩.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨0,-z,2y⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2y)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3y-\\frac{4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}(-2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y-\\frac{4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186405094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405091 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d8800b1d-0dbb-5dd9-8914-c007ddb67ebc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405092 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405092 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405092 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "86b9be73-bab1-55d5-99f8-7629e8fdfac0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405093 #edb/ref 1080 "2y+\\frac{4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405093 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405093 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03b65f71-c8ab-568a-a5b4-8a9e1e082302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405094 #edb/ref 1080 "y-\\frac{4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405094 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405094 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a7ec3f6d-843d-5ada-bec6-0a99ea632881" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405095 #edb/ref 1080 "4y+\\frac{2y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405095 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405095 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "62a9e402-0459-5909-abf2-55ce70fd1f54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405096 #edb/ref 1080 "y-\\frac{2y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405096 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405096 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c486fa33-cd09-56ea-8bcb-3f7d7b5b1b6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405097 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186405098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405097 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161904" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405097 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405097 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $F=⟨-y,\\,0,\\,x⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that encloses the finite region between the hemisphere $z=1-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ and the plane $z=1.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich expression belongs in the blank when the upper and lower surfaces are parametrized as graphs over $D$ and their outward flux integrands are added pointwise where defined, before integration?" #edb/ref 17592186045423] [17592186405097 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "150a753b-c416-5943-8cfa-2d89a5b17df4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405097 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=1$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=1-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper plane ${S}_{1}.$\n\nSince the positive orientation is upward, the unit normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,0,1⟩.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨-y,0,x⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider lower hemisphere ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=-y,\\,Q=0,\\,R=x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is downward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂h}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-(-y)\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-(0)\\cdot \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{D}(\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x-\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045423] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186405103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186405099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405098 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4cf9dad5-46da-52ad-9f58-b7b22be13881" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405099 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405099 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186405099 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e0745c0-c1e3-54ed-89c3-84df7cb535ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
